      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "SWAN STUDIOS - VIDEO TO CHARACTER  (face + body, runs on YOUR 5090)\n\nDrop a VIDEO in, point at two frames, and generate that person - face\nAND body - in any scene you type. No outside tools; ComfyUI extracts\nthe frames itself.\n\nHOW TO USE\n  0. LONG VIDEO? Trim it first - that is the DEFAULT PROTOCOL:\n     drag the video onto 'Swan Trim Clip' on the Desktop, type the\n     start and end (like 7:00 and 7:20), and the clip lands in this\n     workflow's video dropdown automatically (refresh the browser).\n     The trim re-encodes to constant 24fps so cut times AND the\n     index = seconds x 24 arithmetic are exact even for phone video.\n  1. Node V: choose your video (SHORT clips only - see law 1).\n  2. Node P1 (FACE frame) + P2 (BODY frame): set batch_index to pick\n     the frames. Arithmetic: index = seconds x fps (usually 24).\n     Every Run also SAVES the two picked frames next to the result,\n     so you can see what you chose and adjust.\n  3. Node 8: describe the new scene. Start with 'The same woman/man'.\n  4. Run. ~20s cold, ~6s when only a pick changed (unchanged nodes\n     are cached).\n\nLAWS LEARNED BY EXECUTION (2026-09-02)\n  1. SHORT CLIPS ONLY - the whole video decodes into memory. Under\n     ~20s is safe at 1280x704. Trim a long video first.\n  2. FACE frame = a normal head-and-shoulders view. An extreme\n     close-up (one eye) makes the model compose collages.\n  3. AVOID frames with on-screen text - it LEAKS into the render\n     (a title card printed its slogan into the output).\n  4. BODY frame = the person clearly visible head to toe, alone if\n     possible - other people in frame can ride along into the result.\n\nFACE + BODY - the honest ladder\n  - One face frame: face carries, body approximate.\n  - Face + body frame (THIS graph): face and build/outfit both carry.\n  - The permanent lock is still a character LoRA trained on 20-30\n    varied stills - build those WITH this graph, then train (see\n    Install-Krea2-Training-NOTES.md).\n\nRecipe: 8 steps / cfg 1.0 / euler / simple. Seed FIXED - bump it for\nvariations. Same aspect law as 05: keep output 1280x704."
      ],
      "title": "Note"
    }
